> The secretary record model

In a uniform random permutation of n distinct candidates, the event that
position i sets a new record has probability1/i; these record indicators are
independent. Selecting the last record is equivalent to selecting the overall
best candidate. This particular model satisfies the odds theorem’s assumptions.
The relation does not justify applying the rule to arbitrary dependent sequences
of observed ranks.

For i≥2 the odds are1/(i−1). Summing their tail to1 places the threshold near
n/e, while the optimal probability approaches1/e. The table preserves the
original n=10,100,1000 studies; the plot compares their actual finite-n values
with the asymptotic constant, without reporting asymptotic equality at finite n.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/odds_secretary.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| events n | actual threshold | threshold/n | actual win probability | actual suffix visits " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {10, 100, 1000}) {
        auto r =
            dm::algorithms::odds_algorithm_run(dm::algorithms::odds_secretary_probabilities(n));
        x.push_back(std::log10(double(n)));
        y.push_back(r.result.win_probability);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {:.9f} | {:.12f} | {} |\n", n,
                   r.result.threshold, double(r.result.threshold) / n,
                   r.result.win_probability, r.visits);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(x, y, "finite-n value", dm::graphics::RGBA{37, 99, 235, 255}).points(x, y, dm::graphics::RGBA{37, 99, 235, 255}, 3.).abline_h(1 / std::exp(1.), dm::graphics::RGB{220, 38, 38}, 2);
    p.title("Secretary record events: finite-n last-success value").x_label(
        "log10(number of candidates)").y_label("actual computed win probability").y_limits(.36, .415).save_svg("build/odds_secretary.svg");
}
```
