> Certain events, complete validation and ownership

The previous producer treated p=1 as zero odds. For a sole certain event it
consequently reported zero win probability, although stopping there wins surely.
The corrected producer flags a certain event, terminates at it if reached, and
computes W through the nonsingular recurrence. For two certain events the
selected threshold is the later one. Zero probabilities, empty inputs and ties
remain explicit controls.

All probabilities, including an unvisited prefix, must be finite and belong
to[0,1]. Validation precedes adaptive work. Empty input retains the historical
threshold0/probability0 convention; a nonempty all-zero input returns
threshold1/probability0. A trace owns all input values plus the actual visited
suffix records. Its logical quota counts n+2+visits, default1000000, zero
disabling; complete input/result admission and online record admission precede
copying. This is not bytes or a peak-memory estimate. Ordinary validation and
traversal take O(n) time and constant working storage; a trace takes O(n+visits)
owned storage. The separate curve requires O(n) work and n+1 output rows.

Wide arithmetic reduces avoidable singularities but does not certify rounding
error, a uniquely optimal threshold near a tie, or validity under dependence.
The invariant probabilities and optimality statement concern the stated
independent-event model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/odds_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<std::vector<double>> inputs{{}, {0., 0.}, {1.}, {1., 1.},
                                            {1., 0., 0.}, {.5, .5}};
    std::vector<std::string> labels{"empty", "zeros", "certain", "two certain",
                                    "certain then zeros", "tie"};
    std::vector<double> wins;
    std::print("| control | actual threshold | actual win probability | certain stop | actual visits | " "captured units |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < inputs.size(); ++i) {
        auto t = dm::algorithms::odds_algorithm_trace(inputs[i]);
        wins.push_back(t.run.result.win_probability);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", labels[i],
                   t.run.result.threshold, t.run.result.win_probability,
                   t.run.certain, t.run.visits, t.captured_entries);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(wins, labels, "actual win chance");
    p.title("Last-success controls: zero, certain and tied events").x_label(
        "explicit probability model").y_label("computed win probability").y_limits(0, 1.2).save_svg("build/odds_controls.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| control | actual threshold | actual win probability | certain stop | actual visits | captured units |
| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |
| empty | 0 | 0 | false | 0 | 2 |
| zeros | 1 | 0 | false | 2 | 6 |
| certain | 1 | 1 | true | 1 | 4 |
| two certain | 2 | 1 | true | 1 | 5 |
| certain then zeros | 1 | 1 | true | 3 | 8 |
| tie | 2 | 0.5 | false | 1 | 5 |
\image(figures/odds_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual empty, impossible, certain and tied-event controls from the corrected canonical producer.)
\alttext(A certain last eligible success has win probability1; empty and all-zero inputs have win probability0.)

[Bruss(2000), Sum the odds to one and stop|https://doi.org/10.1214/aop/1019160340]
gives the independent-event optimal stopping theorem. The recurrence and
threshold comparison above explain the quantities produced here; no external
observations or estimated event probabilities are introduced.

> Verification

This ten-report batch passes 50 CTest cases, 25 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases, 174 compiled and executed public examples, 707/707 scoped documentation
definitions and ten representative clangd hovers. Independent Python checks
verify 5662 records with 27916 checks: optimal prefix-code costs, train-only
Titanic category counts and held-out confusion, and all 5001 actual original
Lorenz RK4 steps. Frozen valid-input comparisons cover all ten producers, with
intentional guard, ownership, arithmetic and endpoint corrections stated
separately. Twelve checkout headers and twelve byte-identical installed
development headers compile independently; an installed-header native consumer
links and runs. All 40 complete programs execute, and 40 native figures have
been visually reviewed. HTML/Markdown exports preserve computed results and
image bytes. These are scoped native checks. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-264-273/`.
